<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maeda clan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Maeda clan was a Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> family that ruled the Kaga domain, the largest domain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-period">Edo period</a>, assessed at over one million koku. Its founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maeda-toshiie">Maeda Toshiie</a> served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>, and his son Toshinaga backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> in 1600. Watched closely as outside lords, the Maeda spent heavily on culture, making <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanazawa">Kanazawa</a> a centre of crafts and learning.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maeda-clan.jpg" alt="Maeda clan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mukai · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Japanese_crest_Kaga_Umebachi.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
